results.carrier_model:
CREATION: nova_rt_main_dispatch (line 4577) becomes the M:N bootstrap. Instead of calling nova_rt_sched_run() on the main thread, it: (1) determines N = min(cpu_count, NOVA_WS_MAX_WORKERS), overridable by NOVA_CARRIERS env var; (2) initializes N NovaCarrier structs in a global array g_carriers[NOVA_WS_MAX_WORKERS]; (3) spawns the root task onto carrier-0's deque; (4) launches N-1 OS threads (carrier-1..N-1), each running nova_carrier_loop; (5) the main thread itself runs nova_carrier_loop as carrier-0. Each carrier thread calls nova_ensure_carrier() on entry (already thread-local safe, lines 3785-3798) to convert itself to a fiber.

CARRIER STRUCT (replaces the flat globals at lines 4121-4127):
```
typedef struct NovaCarrier {
    int id;
    NovaWSDeque deque;              // per-carrier work-stealing deque
    NovaIOWaiter* io_waiters;       // I/O parked tasks (this carrier only)
    NovaSleepWaiter* sleep_waiters; // sleep parked tasks (this carrier only)
    NovaOffloadJob* offload_waiters;// offload parked tasks (this carrier only)
    // padding to avoid false sharing (128 bytes between hot fields)
    char _pad[64];
    #ifdef _WIN32
    HANDLE thread;
    #else
    pthread_t thread;
    #endif
    volatile int active;
} NovaCarrier;
```

THREAD-LOCAL nova_sched_current: The global `static NovaSchedTask* nova_sched_current` (line 4123) becomes `__thread NovaSchedTask* nova_sched_current` (or `__declspec(thread)` on Windows). Each carrier sets it before resuming a task and clears it after. This is already the pattern: line 4524 sets, line 4527 clears. The thread-local nova_current_fiber and nova_carrier_fiber (lines 3774-3780) are ALREADY thread-local, so each carrier already gets its own fiber context.

THREAD-LOCAL carrier ID: A new `__thread int nova_carrier_id = -1` lets any code running on a carrier know WHICH carrier it's on, needed for local-deque push and for I/O/sleep waiter registration.

PINNING: Tasks are NOT pinned. When a task yields (parks on I/O, sleep, channel, or offload), it gets re-enqueued by whichever carrier scans the relevant waiter list. Since waiter lists are per-carrier (see shared_state_plan), the carrier that scanned the waiter re-enqueues to ITS OWN deque, so the task runs on the scanner -- natural migration.

ROOT TASK + MAIN: The root task (nova_main) is spawned onto carrier-0. nova_rt_main_dispatch waits for all carriers to finish (the main thread IS carrier-0, so it returns when carrier-0's loop exits). Termination condition: when nova_sched_live (now atomic) reaches 0, all carriers observe it and exit. The root task's exit status is checked as today (line 4586).

CARRIER LOOP (replaces nova_rt_sched_run at line 4501):
```
while (!g_sched_shutdown) {
    // 1. Wake local sleepers
    nova_carrier_wake_sleepers(me);
    // 2. Check local offload completions
    nova_carrier_check_offload(me);
    // 3. Pop from local deque
    NovaSchedTask* t = ws_deque_pop(&me->deque);
    // 4. If empty, try global overflow queue
    if (!t) t = global_rq_steal();
    // 5. If still empty, steal from random victim
    if (!t) t = steal_from_random(me);
    // 6. If still empty, poll I/O (blocking with timeout)
    if (!t && (me->io_waiters || me->sleep_waiters || me->offload_waiters)) {
        nova_carrier_poll_io(me, 1/*ms*/);
        nova_carrier_wake_sleepers(me);
        nova_carrier_check_offload(me);
        t = ws_deque_pop(&me->deque);
    }
    // 7. If truly idle, brief sleep then retry
    if (!t) { if (atomic_load(&nova_sched_live) <= 0) break; Sleep(1); continue; }
    // 8. Run the task
    nova_sched_current = t;
    t->status = 1;
    int64_t done = nova_rt_fiber_resume(t->fiber);
    nova_sched_current = NULL;
    // 9. Handle completion / re-enqueue / park (same as lines 4528-4555)
}
```
